Physical Layer Failure:
Unauthorized USB devices were allowed to be connected to the workstation.

Missing Control:
USB Device Control / Removable Media Restriction


Technical Layer Failure (Endpoint):
The system executed a script from the USB drive without restriction.

Missing Control:
Application Whitelisting or Endpoint Protection


Technical Layer Failure (Network):
The attacker logged in remotely using a stolen password.

Missing Control:
Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)


Administrative Layer Failure:
The employee plugged in an unknown USB device due to lack of awareness.

Missing Control:
Security Awareness Training
